ar scenery and  building elements like a normal person  then you can definitely experiment a bit  with coaster track to make some elements  that would otherwise be really difficult  to make I have to say I also didn't make  it too easy on myself by trying to build  what I'm trying to build which is some  kind of classical Renaissance building  with a traditional front with the  pediments pillars architrave frieze  etcetera with the dome behind it which  we'll get to in a minute this is  definitely not the easiest thing to  build with roller coaster tracks so  maybe I could have made my own life a  bit easier but I just really wanted to  try this especially after I had the idea  to twist different rollercoaster tracks  into each other to make the pillars and  to make the pillars actually look like  they have these grooves that they do in  real life which I think works out pretty  well I think  for me at least the thing that mostly  sells this build is the fact that the  pillars look pretty decent if you don't  count the their tops and bottoms which  are a bit weird anyway I skipped ahead a  bit here to go into my experimentation  with the dome that's going to be on top  of the building and this was actually a  little bit less of a struggle I think  than most detailing because  rollercoaster tracks of course are very  good at making curves so making the dome  wasn't too annoying the the bad part  about this is yet to come and that is  trying to get different pieces to line  up to actually make a dome structure  rather than just a two-dimensional  diamond cut out but yeah so far is so  good honestly now another thing that  made this really difficult eventually is  the fact that you can't move stuff  around like you can with regular scenery  pieces which is enough of a struggle  while you're still building but it  becomes really difficult to alter your  building after you're done putting  things in place and that I think was the  major struggle and making this building 