st the the skill  struggle that I had trying to build a  building out of coaster track I don't  think I could have made it smaller and  still make it look believable so I'm  just going to try and scale up anything  I can so these windows are also really  large any of the detailing that I'll add  around it will be really large and the  foliage then I'll add in the end will  also be made pretty much exclusively out  of some of the biggest trees in the game  just to make this thing feel believable  I know that sounds like cheating a bit  but I think without the the bigger scale  it would have been completely undoable  that was definitely one of my other  breaking points then I had to consider  se-young copying this window around just  to make the building look a bit more  believable which I think it does a fair  job ads but then I was trying to fill it  into the dome section here and I  realized that the window was much too  large for that so I decided to set one  window apart and try to work on it a bit  make it a bit more narrow and possibly  its hauler and just change the overall  design of it because typically  especially with these kinds of  neoclassical buildings you'll have  different orders on different floors of  the building so because I have these  arched windows on the ground floor  wanted to have different type of windows  on the second floor here or the first  floor depending on where you're from and  what it all means anyway just underneath  the dome and yeah just decided to go for  some simple rectangular windows which on  their own don't work too well but they  fit very snugly between the pillars of  the domed section of the building and I  think it works very well it just in  general it makes that whole section look  better although I also have to say on  these windows especially it becomes very  clear that these are made out of roller  coaster track so especially for this  dome section you definitely want to zoom  out a bit to keep that suspense of  